This project contains software, hardware design files, and documentation.
Those are different kinds of work, and each is licensed under the licence
written for it. Full texts are in LICENSES/.

  Software and firmware        MIT                  LICENSES/MIT.txt
  Hardware and enclosure       CERN-OHL-P-2.0       LICENSES/CERN-OHL-P-2.0.txt
  Documentation and images     CC-BY-4.0            LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

All three are permissive. None of them requires you to open your own work.


WHICH LICENCE APPLIES TO WHICH FILE

Stated by path, because "hardware files" and "documentation" are ambiguous at
the edges and a path is not.

  MIT
    firmware/          Arduino sketches
    host/              Python daemon, tests and configuration
    hooks/             Claude Code hook helpers
    scripts/           PowerShell install and uninstall scripts
    anything not listed below

  CERN-OHL-P-2.0
    enclosure/         SolidWorks sources, STEP exports and 3MF meshes

  CC-BY-4.0
    docs/              All documentation
    photos/            Photographs of the build
    README.md          and any other Markdown at the repository root


CODE INSIDE DOCUMENTATION IS MIT

The documentation is full of code: pin definitions, register writes, shell
commands, configuration snippets. Those samples are MIT, not CC-BY-4.0. Copy
them into your own project without attributing anything. The prose around them
is CC-BY-4.0, so quote or adapt that with credit.

This carve-out exists because the alternative is absurd. Nobody should have to
attribute a four-line function they copied out of a troubleshooting guide.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Third-party libraries, fonts and other components keep their own licences.
Nothing here relicenses them. The dependencies this project builds against are
all permissive:

  Adafruit GFX Library                      BSD
  Adafruit ST7735 and ST7789 Library        BSD
  Adafruit BusIO                            MIT
  ArduinoJson                               MIT
  pyserial                                  BSD
  pytest                                    MIT
